            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The World of Numbers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.855,
            0.069,
            0.884,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "45"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.11,
            0.643,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3 Integers: Expanding the Horizon"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.143,
            0.885,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Brahmagupta did not stop at zero. He realised that if subtraction of a number from itself can result in zero (5 – 5 = 0), then what would happen if we subtracted a larger number from a smaller one "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(3 - 5 =  口 ) ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.202,
            0.885,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To answer this, Brahmagupta grounded his mathematics in the reality of commerce and life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.241,
            0.432,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "He recognised two states:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.262,
            0.883,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fortunes (Dhana):",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Positive numbers, representing wealth or assets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.286,
            0.758,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Debts (Ṛiṇa):",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Negative numbers, representing debts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.314,
            0.886,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By moving to the left of zero on the number line, Brahmagupta formally introduced "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Negative Numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the world. The combination of positive natural numbers, their negative counterparts, and zero creates the set of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Integers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", denoted by the symbol Z (from the German word Zahlen, meaning numbers)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.428,
            0.863,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.134,
                0.428,
                0.863,
                0.524
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.465,
                0.535,
                0.534,
                0.552
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 3.2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.587,
            0.521,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3.1 The Arithmetic of Integers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.616,
            0.885,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Brahmagupta gave explicit rules for adding and multiplying these integers, which we still use exactly as he wrote them over 1,300 years ago:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.665,
            0.695,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A fortune plus a fortune is a fortune:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 5 + 4 = 9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.693,
            0.884,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A debt plus a debt is a debt:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (– 5) + (– 4) = –9. (If you owe `5 and borrow `4 more, you owe `9.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.743,
            0.884,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A fortune minus zero is a fortune, a debt minus zero is a debt:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 - 0 = 7, \\mathrm{and} - 6 - 0 = - 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.787,
            0.883,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The product of a debt and a fortune is a debt:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-3) \\times 4 = -12"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (If you take on 4 debts of `3, your total debt is `12.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.833,
            0.776,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The product of two debts is a fortune:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 3 ) \\times ( - 4 ) = 12"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
